> Task :populateArtifactURLs
Updated `metadata/org.apache.pulsar/pulsar-client-all/index.json`: filled the missing `documentation-url` with `https://pulsar.apache.org/docs/4.2.x/`, the version-pinned docs portal for the 4.2.x release line containing 4.2.5 (verified via WebFetch — explicit "Version: 4.2.x" selector, not a `latest`/`next` redirect).

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
- I didn't templatize the docs URL with `$version$` even though the task prefers templates: Pulsar's doc site groups releases by minor line (`4.2.x`), not by exact patch version, so the tested-version alias `4.2.5` never appears as a literal substring in the URL. Substituting `$version$` → `4.2.5` would produce a broken `.../docs/4.2.5/` path. The task's own rule — "only when that template is valid for every alias" — is exactly the guardrail that rules this out, so a literal, non-templated URL is the correct choice here.
- `language` stayed absent rather than being set to `"N/A"`: the two sentinels mean different things. `"N/A"` says "I looked for this and couldn't confirm it", which fits URLs/description. `language` is different — it's conditionally applicable (only for Kotlin/Scala/Groovy artifacts), so "not applicable" is correctly expressed by omitting the key entirely, not by writing a value into it.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

The other four fields (`source-code-url`, `repository-url`, `test-code-url`, `description`) already held non-blank values, so per the instructions I left them untouched — including `test-code-url`, which still points at `pulsar-client/src/test` rather than `pulsar-client-all` (the shaded packaging module has no distinct test suite of its own; that's a pre-existing editorial choice, not something this task asked me to fix).
